+# External review, round 8 (condensed record)
+
+Received 2026-11-09 on the round-8 package (22 files, all read; the 15 unchanged files byte-identical to round 7).
+
+- **Verdict:** submit to WEIS; the round-7 submission condition is resolved. Scores unchanged: AAMAS main 2/5, WEIS 2027
+  4/5, EC 1/5, confidence 4/5 at each. Forecasts: AAMAS 30% (35% after a venue edit), WEIS 70% (75%), EC 5% (6%).
+- **Eligibility audit:** all five tallies reproduced from the 70 scored cells and 21 flags with zero discrepancies
+  (direct 10/8/0, 7/8/3, 6/5/7; traced 10/8/0, 6/8/4, 5/4/9). Q3-e and Q2-d explain the direct-versus-traced difference.
+  Tracing is a conservative sensitivity to recorded provenance, not proof of causal influence (for a same-reference
+  contrast the reference payoff cancels). The six exemptions are defensible as a post hoc convention; Q4-b is a
+  diagnostic about decisions, not a confirmatory decision.
+- **New problems (text only):** (1) "searches each prediction cell requires" overstates the trace; say recorded
+  ancestors, an inherited flag does not show selection or a changed statistic. (2) The broader rule excludes cells, not
+  whole predictions, and the six exemptions are "decision-related"; rename the reading "all non-exempt cells". (3)
+  Separate the original numerical scoring path from the revised script; put both direct-input tallies in Table 21.
+- **Remaining work:** text edits above; move the eligibility table near its paragraph (venue layout); at release, a
+  manifest with root ids and parent-child hashes; optional cross-play comparison for AAMAS. No new simulation, compute,
+  or review round before WEIS.
